n\\nb\\n' | nl` → `     1\\ta\\n\\n     2\\tb\\n`\n     - Non-goals: no locale-aware collation for regex, Go regexp used directly\n   \n   - **cmd/nl/main.go** (existing stub, needs modification)\n     - Already has: options struct, defaultOptions(), parseArgs(), parseFlag(), setStyle(), setStringOpt(), setIntOpt(), run(), processFile()\n     - **Critical bug in processInput() (lines 196-208)**: Numbers ALL lines including empty ones, and lineNum is local so it resets between files\n     ```go\n     func processInput(r io.Reader, opts options) error {\n         w := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n         scanner := bufio.NewScanner(r)\n         lineNum := opts.startNum\n         for scanner.Scan() {\n             line := scanner.Text()\n             if _, err := fmt.Fprintf(w, \"%*d%s%s\\n\", opts.width, lineNum, opts.separator, line); err != nil {\n                 return err\n             }\n             lineNum += opts.increment\n         }\n         return w.Flush()\n     }\n     ```\n     - run() function (lines 55-75) calls processFile in a loop but doesn't share lineNum state\n     - Options struct has all fields for R1-R4: bodyStyle, headerStyle, footerStyle, numberFormat, width, separator, startNum, increment, delimiter, noReset, joinBlankCount\n   \n   - **cmd/nl/nl_test.go** (existing skeleton, needs DiffTest entries)\n     - Has TestDiff with empty `tests := []testutils.DiffTest{}`\n     - Has TestSIGPIPE already implemented\n     - Uses `exec.LookPath(\"gnl\")` with skip on missing\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was in the reading/planning phase when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that processInput() needs major rework: (a) empty lines must pass through unnumbered, (b) lineNum must be shared across files for R1.4, (c) need to use numbering style (default \"t\" = non-empty only for body)\n   - The run() function needs to pass a shared counter or restructure so lineNum persists across processFile calls\n   - 