{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WMy1hrTAiYfWWW2DUxND5f","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I found all the information you requested. Here's the summary:\n\n## DiffTest Struct Definition\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      int\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n## RunDiffTests Function Signature\n\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n```\n\n## How the ExpectedFiles Field Works\n\nThe `ExpectedFiles` field is a `map[string][]byte` that maps relative file paths to their expected byte content. Here's how it's used:\n\n1. **In the test flow**: After both binaries execute, the `checkExpectedFiles` function (lines 211-227) validates the files created by the command.\n\n2. **File checking logic**:\n   - If `ExpectedFiles` is nil, the check is skipped (line 213-214)\n   - For each relative path in the map, it constructs the full path by joining it with the working directory\n   - It reads the actual file content using `os.ReadFile`\n   - It compares the actual content with the expected content using `bytes.Equal`\n   - If the file doesn't exist or the content doesn't match, the test fails with a detailed error message\n\nThis allows you to verify that commands produce expected files with specific content during differential testing.\n\nThe file is located at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5257/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc814666-c3c1-43ab-8b2c-3e158e561013","uuid":"e6cf51d7-c947-44c4-8913-75f8fa184a54","timestamp":"2026-05-15T03:34:14.909Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find the DiffTest struct definition in pkg/testutils/ in the go-unix-utils repo at /private